## 5. Physical Network Topology

A network topology describes how devices are physically or logically connected.

### 5.1 Star Topology

In a star topology, devices connect to a central switch.

```text
                  ROUTER
                     |
                     |
                   SWITCH
              /      |      \
             /       |       \
          SERVER   DESKTOP   ACCESS POINT
```

Advantages:

- Easy to understand.
- Simple to expand.
- Individual device connections can be diagnosed.
- A problem with one endpoint cable normally does not disconnect every other endpoint.

A central switch failure, however, can affect all devices connected through it.

### 5.2 Proposed Initial Physical Topology

```text
                 INTERNET
                     |
                  ISP MODEM
                     |
                   ROUTER
                     |
                  SWITCH
                     |
              +------+------+
              |      |      |
           SERVER  PC/LAPTOP  NAS
              |
          NETWORK PORT
              |
        SERVER OPERATING
           PLATFORM
              |
       VIRTUAL NETWORK
              |
        +-----+------+
        |     |      |
       VM1   VM2    VM3
```

The initial physical network should remain simple.

Start with the router, one switch if required, a server and an administration computer.

Additional network devices can be introduced when the lab has a clear requirement for them.

