## 11. Physical Server Networking

The physical server connects the virtualization platform or operating system to the physical network.

### 11.1 Single NIC Configuration

A simple design can use one physical Ethernet interface.

```text
             PHYSICAL SERVER
                    |
                 NIC 1
                    |
                ETHERNET
                    |
              NETWORK SWITCH
```

Advantages:

- Simple setup.
- Lower hardware cost.
- Suitable for a basic home lab.

Limitations:

- One physical connection carries the relevant traffic.
- A single NIC or cable failure can disconnect the server.
- Management and workload traffic may share one physical link.

Logical separation using VLANs may still be possible when the switch, router and server configuration support it.

### 11.2 Multiple NIC Configuration

A server with multiple network interfaces can provide more flexibility.

```text
              PHYSICAL SERVER
                    |
          +---------+---------+
          |                   |
         NIC 1               NIC 2
          |                   |
     MANAGEMENT            WORKLOADS
          |                   |
          +---------+---------+
                    |
              NETWORK SWITCH
```

This is an illustrative logical arrangement, not a mandatory cabling design.

Possible benefits include:

- Separating selected traffic types.
- Increasing available network bandwidth.
- Building dedicated storage or management networks.
- Providing redundancy when properly configured.

Multiple NICs do not automatically provide higher availability. Redundancy requires compatible configuration, switching and network design.

### 11.3 Link Aggregation

Link aggregation combines multiple compatible physical network links into one logical connection.

It may be used for:

- Higher aggregate bandwidth across multiple traffic flows.
- Link redundancy.
- Network infrastructure design.

Both ends must support and correctly configure the selected aggregation method.

Link aggregation does not normally make one individual connection faster than the speed of one physical link.

