## 17. Network Monitoring

Monitoring provides visibility into network health and performance.

Useful measurements include:

- Link status.
- Link speed.
- Bandwidth usage.
- Packet loss.
- Latency.
- Interface errors.
- Connected device availability.
- DNS response.
- Service availability.

### 17.1 Example Monitoring Plan

| Component | What to monitor |
|---|---|
| Router | Availability and internet connectivity |
| Switch | Port status and link speed |
| Server NIC | Link state, traffic and errors |
| Virtual machines | Network connectivity |
| DNS service | Resolution success |
| DHCP service | Address assignment |
| Firewall | Blocked and allowed traffic |
| Internet link | Availability and latency |

### 17.2 Monitoring Tools

Examples of tools that may be useful:

- Wireshark — packet analysis.
- tcpdump — command-line packet capture.
- Netdata — system and infrastructure monitoring.
- Prometheus — metrics collection.
- Grafana — metrics visualization.
- Zabbix — infrastructure monitoring.
- LibreNMS — network monitoring.

Select tools according to the scale of the lab.

Packet captures and monitoring logs can contain sensitive information. Review them before sharing publicly.

