## 21. Network Implementation Roadmap

Build the network in stages. Do not start with unnecessary complexity.

### Phase 1: Basic Connectivity

- [ ] Identify the router.
- [ ] Identify the existing home network subnet.
- [ ] Identify the DHCP range.
- [ ] Identify the server Ethernet interface.
- [ ] Connect the server by Ethernet.
- [ ] Confirm that the server receives a valid IP address.
- [ ] Test communication with the router.
- [ ] Test internet connectivity.
- [ ] Document the working configuration.

### Phase 2: Infrastructure Addressing

- [ ] Select a server hostname.
- [ ] Select a predictable server IP.
- [ ] Configure a static IP or DHCP reservation.
- [ ] Record the network configuration.
- [ ] Confirm that there are no address conflicts.
- [ ] Test access from the administration computer.

### Phase 3: Server and Virtual Machine Networking

- [ ] Configure the server network.
- [ ] Configure the virtualization bridge if a hypervisor is selected.
- [ ] Create one test VM.
- [ ] Connect the VM to the intended virtual network.
- [ ] Verify VM connectivity.
- [ ] Verify that firewall rules are understood.

### Phase 4: Network Segmentation

Only after the basic network is stable:

- [ ] Confirm router VLAN support.
- [ ] Confirm managed switch VLAN support.
- [ ] Design VLAN IDs and subnets.
- [ ] Define access and trunk ports.
- [ ] Configure VLAN routing.
- [ ] Configure firewall policies.
- [ ] Test each network segment.
- [ ] Test permitted and blocked communication paths.
- [ ] Document the final configuration.

### Phase 5: Advanced Networking

- [ ] Add a separate management network if required.
- [ ] Implement a dedicated lab network.
- [ ] Evaluate network storage requirements.
- [ ] Configure monitoring.
- [ ] Evaluate VPN-based remote access.
- [ ] Test recovery from network configuration errors.
- [ ] Review security and performance.

