## 22. Network Acceptance Checklist

The network should meet the following basic requirements before it is considered operational.

### Physical Connectivity

- [ ] Router is operational.
- [ ] Switch is operational, if used.
- [ ] Server Ethernet connection is active.
- [ ] Administration computer is connected.
- [ ] No obvious cable or link problems remain.

### IP Configuration

- [ ] Server has a valid IP address.
- [ ] Subnet configuration is correct.
- [ ] Default gateway is correct.
- [ ] DNS resolution works.
- [ ] No known duplicate IP addresses exist.

### Server Connectivity

- [ ] Administration computer can reach the server.
- [ ] Server can reach the gateway.
- [ ] Server can access required network services.
- [ ] Remote administration works if enabled.
- [ ] Virtual machine networking works if configured.

### Security

- [ ] Management interfaces are restricted.
- [ ] Unnecessary internet exposure is avoided.
- [ ] Firewall policies are documented.
- [ ] Guest network isolation is reviewed where applicable.
- [ ] Credentials and sensitive information are not stored in public documentation.

